      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "62a42265-c6a0-4106-99b2-0197c6b665b8",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "1. Access the University Catalog for Programs and Degrees, General Education Requirements, and Graduation Requirements at CSUCI. 2. Access the Program Website and Program Information in the University Catalog. 3. Access Transfer 2-year or Freshman 4-year Academic Roadmaps. 4. Access the Admissions website for CSUCI admission requirements. 5. Access the Transfer Credit website for information about Associate Degrees for Transfer, and transfer credit resources for external exams and U.S. Military service. 6. Learn more About CSUCI . Articulation agreements are subject to change from one academic year to the next. It is recommended to review the applicable department agreement(s) in addition to the major agreement and that students meet with a counselor/academic advisor early and often during their academic career.",
      "contentHtml": "<p>1.&nbsp;Access&nbsp;the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://catalog.csuci.edu/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">University&nbsp;Catalog</a>&nbsp;for&nbsp;Programs&nbsp;and&nbsp;Degrees,&nbsp;General&nbsp;Education&nbsp;Requirements,&nbsp;and&nbsp;Graduation&nbsp;Requirements&nbsp;at&nbsp;CSUCI.</p><p>2.&nbsp;Access&nbsp;the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://spanish.csuci.edu/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Program&nbsp;Website</a>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<a href=\"https://catalog.csuci.edu/preview_entity.php?catoid=64&amp;ent_oid=3932&amp;returnto=8136\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Program&nbsp;Information</a>&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;University&nbsp;Catalog.</p><p>3.&nbsp;Access&nbsp;<a href=\"https://catalog.csuci.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=64&amp;poid=17240&amp;returnto=8136\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Transfer&nbsp;2-year</a>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<a href=\"https://catalog.csuci.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=64&amp;poid=17239&amp;returnto=8136\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Freshman&nbsp;4-year</a>&nbsp;Academic&nbsp;Roadmaps.&nbsp;</p><p>4.&nbsp;Access&nbsp;the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.csuci.edu/admissions/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Admissions</a>&nbsp;website&nbsp;for&nbsp;CSUCI&nbsp;admission&nbsp;requirements.</p><p>5.&nbsp;Access&nbsp;the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.csuci.edu/registrar/transfer-credit.htm\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Transfer&nbsp;Credit</a>&nbsp;website&nbsp;for&nbsp;information&nbsp;about&nbsp;Associate&nbsp;Degrees&nbsp;for&nbsp;Transfer,&nbsp;and&nbsp;transfer&nbsp;credit&nbsp;resources&nbsp;for&nbsp;external&nbsp;exams&nbsp;and&nbsp;U.S.&nbsp;Military&nbsp;service.</p><p>6.&nbsp;Learn&nbsp;more&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.csuci.edu/about/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">About&nbsp;CSUCI</a>.</p><p></p><p>Articulation&nbsp;agreements&nbsp;are&nbsp;subject&nbsp;to&nbsp;change&nbsp;from&nbsp;one&nbsp;academic&nbsp;year&nbsp;to&nbsp;the&nbsp;next.&nbsp;It&nbsp;is&nbsp;recommended&nbsp;to&nbsp;review&nbsp;the&nbsp;applicable&nbsp;department&nbsp;agreement(s)&nbsp;in&nbsp;addition&nbsp;to&nbsp;the&nbsp;major&nbsp;agreement&nbsp;and&nbsp;that&nbsp;students&nbsp;meet&nbsp;with&nbsp;a&nbsp;counselor/academic&nbsp;advisor&nbsp;early&nbsp;and&nbsp;often&nbsp;during&nbsp;their&nbsp;academic&nbsp;career.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "3a4b2851-c262-417f-80b0-0197c6b762ee",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "GENERAL INFORMATION",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "85058082-41ce-476c-bf1c-0197c788df2c",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "1. The following applies to the Lower Division Requirements sections below: 1. Students who enter the SETI program with the equivalent of first-year, college-level Spanish in high school or a community college may have satisfied the SPAN 101 and SPAN 102 requirement. For more information, see the SETI Program Faculty Advisor or the following webpages: 1. AP, CLEP, IB, and U.S. Military Service Credit: https://www.csuci.edu/registrar/transfer-credit-resources/external-exams.htm 2. For placement guidelines: http://spanish.csuci.edu/plcguidcorsdesc.htm 2. Students must complete one series (6 units) of second-year Spanish courses, either SPAN 201 and 202 or SPAN 211 and SPAN 212. Heritage speakers are encouraged to enroll in SPAN 211 and SPAN 212. Higher level speakers may begin at SPAN 301 or SPAN 302 with faculty advisor approval.",
      "contentHtml": "<p>1. The following applies to the Lower Division Requirements sections below:</p><p class=\"ql-indent-1\">1. Students who enter the SETI program with the equivalent of first-year, college-level Spanish in high school or a community college may have satisfied the SPAN 101 and SPAN 102 requirement. For more information, see the SETI Program Faculty Advisor or the following webpages:</p><p class=\"ql-indent-2\">1. AP, CLEP, IB, and U.S. Military Service Credit: <a href=\"https://www.csuci.edu/registrar/transfer-credit-resources/external-exams.htm\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.csuci.edu/registrar/transfer-credit-resources/external-exams.htm</a></p><p class=\"ql-indent-2\">2. For placement guidelines: <a href=\"https://spanish.csuci.edu/plcguidcorsdesc.htm\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">http://spanish.csuci.edu/plcguidcorsdesc.htm</a></p><p class=\"ql-indent-1\">2. Students must complete one series (6 units) of second-year Spanish courses, either SPAN 201 and 202 or SPAN 211 and SPAN 212. Heritage speakers are encouraged to enroll in SPAN 211 and SPAN 212. Higher level speakers may begin at SPAN 301 or SPAN 302 with faculty advisor approval.</p><p class=\"ql-indent-1\"><br></p>"
    }
  ],
